    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0366" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1497.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Peace
                        Commission.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-31T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 31, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You are hereby instructed to immediately send word to Arias giving him a definite
                    time within which to suspend his military operations at Santiago and any other
                    part of the Republic in which he may be active and to come to Santo Domingo City
                    to lay down his arms and give his allegiance to the Provisional President.
                    Immediately inform the Provisional President of this instruction and obtain from
                    him a written request that American marines be ordered to cooperate with the
                    Customs Guard for the arrest of Arias, basing such action upon the obligation of
                    the United States under the Convention, and arresting him for his complication
                    in smuggling operations in north and seizure of Cutter No. 4 at Monte Cristi.
                    Department considers elimination of Arias necessary to the settlement of
                    conditions in Santo Domingo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
